course: dictionary
lesson: 6305
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have two meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. Morocco is one of them. With a capital M, Morocco is a country in north-west Africa, across the sea from Spain. With a small m, morocco is a fine, soft leather made from goatskin.
explain: Look for clues. «The Strait of Gibraltar is only about 14 km wide at its narrowest, separating Spain in Europe from Morocco in Africa» describes a place on a map, so Morocco means the country. A capital letter in the middle of a sentence is a strong sign that a word is a name.
explain: Then test your choice. Put your meaning back into the sentence. If you read «a cover of country» and it makes no sense, you have picked the wrong meaning. Use the clues around the word, and check that your answer fits.
fact: Morocco (capital M) is a country in north-west Africa, across the sea from Spain.
fact: Morocco has the Atlas Mountains and the Sahara Desert, and cities such as Rabat, Casablanca and Marrakesh.
fact: Morocco (small m) is a fine, soft leather made from goatskin, used for book covers.
fact: The Strait of Gibraltar is only about 14 km wide at its narrowest, and it separates Spain in Europe from Morocco in Africa.
fact: A capital letter shows a name, and the sentence around the word shows which meaning is meant.
exercise: «The Strait of Gibraltar separates Spain from Morocco.» In this sentence, Morocco means | A soft leather for book covers | *A country in Africa | A type of goat | A market selling mint tea
exercise: «The old book had a cover of fine, soft morocco.» What does morocco mean here? | A country across the sea from Spain | *A fine, soft leather made from goatskin | A thick woollen blanket | A city with a big market
exercise: In «Yasmin says the oldest university is in Fez, Morocco», what tells you Morocco is a place name? | The word says | *The capital M and the city Fez just before it | The word oldest | The semicolon
test: What does the capital M in Morocco tell you? | It means the leather is expensive | It is a spelling mistake | *It is the name of a country | It is the start of every sentence
test: A pupil reads «a cover of morocco» and says morocco means the country. Why is she wrong? | *The small m and the word cover show it is leather | Countries never have covers | She is right, it is a country | Book covers are always made of paper
exam: Read «The shoes were made of morocco, and the trip to Morocco took three days.» Which meaning comes first, and which comes second? | Both mean leather | Both mean a city | First country, second leather | *First leather, second country
